#edb/ref 17592186166756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3ea6a3a-8078-5e78-9e2e-c7ecb759b2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{1-3x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3ea6a3a-8078-5e78-9e2e-c7ecb759b2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{1-3x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534808} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cde32a2-c89a-582c-93af-924f59b3619d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "973108cd-4a12-5f7e-8def-c33e7591ffaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-342458" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\sqrt{7}\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-3{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3{x}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2bbc451-3971-5718-9b6a-c792cbf3baa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{x}^{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2bbc451-3971-5718-9b6a-c792cbf3baa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{x}^{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534768} :answer-field/id #uuid "caf30c59-3266-50ba-a4bd-cf968c8851d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0bc32c07-1675-5c17-a61b-a851fe6dbaf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-342471" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{5},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $5{x}^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{5})}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{5})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{10}}\\cdot 5{x}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{1-{x}^{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57d851ce-44b5-5713-ba65-7f5a9cc1122f" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86653cab-377d-5ed8-a471-e37ef1bae183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+(4x+3)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86653cab-377d-5ed8-a471-e37ef1bae183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+(4x+3)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534555} :answer-field/id #uuid "958fb880-28de-5a44-b1da-b802306a2223" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40534571-9b68-5a71-b2eb-96fad07c5254" :question/math-academy-id "q-342666" :question/problem "$$\n\nCalculate ${g}^{′}(x)$ for $g(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3).$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)\\,+$ | $4{e}^{x}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the product rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(u\\cdot v)}{\\text{d}x}={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, chain rule, and  formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3))}^{′} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(4x+3)}^{′} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+\\frac{4{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eaab6e41-d34d-5eca-a41f-5ebe58a6b178" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37c7d91d-cc06-508e-8136-0c7783921fdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x-2)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534372} {:answer/id #uuid "813bb0df-60a0-5317-aae6-74937157ce77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x(x-1)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534545} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba4ffdb-ed17-5ed7-ac4b-60e5e8212467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x-1)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534610} {:answer/id #uuid "b515d758-ad04-57d6-957e-d01e00b0efbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x(2x-1)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534669} {:answer/id #uuid "ece0ec44-e760-591f-b411-d7660b6288df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(2x-1)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ba4ffdb-ed17-5ed7-ac4b-60e5e8212467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x-1)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534610} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d51b538-39cd-589a-b246-54b69d35dae4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd040bd9-e3ef-5708-a352-cc4c61514e23" :question/math-academy-id "q-96426" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x-1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x-1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (2x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4{x}^{2}-4x+1)-1}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-4x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x(x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x-1)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
